cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Reproduction package for "A localisation bound for Standard-Model
  representations in heterotic orbifolds"
message: >-
  If you use this package, please cite both the package and the accompanying
  paper.
type: dataset
version: "2.2"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23575403
date-released: "2026-10-22"
authors:
  - family-names: Ardakanian
    given-names: Navid
    email: n.ardakanian@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent researcher
abstract: >-
  Catalogue inputs, raw orbifolder 1.2.1 output, parsed tables, and every
  analysis script behind the localisation bound on repeated Standard-Model
  representations at heterotic orbifold fixed points. Covers two complete
  catalogues (T^6/(Z2 x Z4) and T^6/(Z3 x Z6): 16,138 distinct models,
  880,589 twisted model-cells, 502,396 fields in a Standard-Model
  representation), a second
  independent implementation of the central counts, the seven-geometry budget
  arithmetic, an independent re-enumeration of the two-class boundary that
  makes the construction exhaustive, the spectra of all nine lattice
  representatives of each of the 4,032 Standard-Model-intact embeddings
  over the two classes (36,288 orbifolder spectra), the explicit
  construction of a model
  realising the configuration the bound permits, and the hidden-SU(2)
  signature with the scope at which it holds. Includes a machine-readable
  claim-to-script map with its resolver, a definitions section fixing every
  counted unit, and a complete log of excluded, failed, duplicate and
  recovered cases.
keywords:
  - heterotic string
  - orbifold compactification
  - Standard Model
  - gauge embedding
  - reproducibility
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"

